WEBVTT

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.130
I wore these colorful clothes for nothing.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.920
They look dull under a sky of this color.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.120
Yeah.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.420
It looks like it might snow or rain.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:35.340
I wonder if the bubble allows 
moisture like snow or rain through.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.560
Actually, if it never rains, 
the humidity will drop,

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.410
and our skin might get drier.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.060
Huh?!

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.030
Thanks for the wonderful forecast, Kotoko!

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.740
I'm going to go moisturize!

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.420
Misa-chan, thanks for helping out.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.900
It's fun with so many cute 
things around, indeed.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:16.300
What's that?

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:17.890
Wanna see?

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.140
Yes, indeed.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.300
Wow...

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.100
They're so sparkly and cute, indeed.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.420
We make accessories with these.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.990
Really? How strange, indeed.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.000
You can turn these sparklies into accessories?

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.370
Scoopers are here! Scoopers are here!

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:50.530
What? Hang on! I'm not 
finished with the cake display!

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.020
Unbelievable. Their timing couldn't be worse.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:57.220
There's a ghost! A ghost! A ghost!

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:02.920
I bet you guys would die 
first in a B horror movie.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.590
I'm going to go check it out.

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:07.140
Wait.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.650
Goodbye, luxury facial mask.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:15.360
I can't put my friends in danger for you.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.420
Mari-chan, you're so nice.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:22.030
I'm like the heroine of 
a major Hollywood movie.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.020
We'll go together.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:36.010
When did Harajuku turn into a safari park?

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.510
Wow...

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.940
There are all kinds of animals.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.250
I want to see the baby lions!

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.650
Stop, Kotoko.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.100
Baby lions certainly are cute,

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.990
but these are all Scoopers.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.460
Oh, right!

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.980
How many are there?

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.660
Stop!

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:30.910
Hey!

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.250
Take this!

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.210
Go away!

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:36.920
Sheesh!

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.010
Misa-sama, watch out!

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.830
Misa-chan, are you okay?

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:51.180
Scoopers, Scoopers!

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.980
Oh, what a cute size.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:02.420
Wait! If you fire in here, 
you'll destroy the shop!

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:03.900
Let's drive it outside first.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.620
<i>They're so sparkly and cute.</i>

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:22.780
Wait!

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:29.930
I'll go after it.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:31.890
Me, too.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.530
Unfortunately for you, 
there's no way out above.

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:40.940
<i>Rito-chan, Mari-chan! It's an emergency!</i>

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.690
What's wrong?

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:47.400
Well, I hacked the security cameras around 
town and found Scoopers all over the place.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:50.480
Sayumin's shop is in trouble, too!

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.570
Are they repainting everything? But...

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:17.900
<i>Wait, Kotoko.</i>

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.260
<i>What's happening to Sayumin?</i>

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:23.690
Oh, well, they stole her colors, 
but Sayumin's okay.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:26.650
Nobody's hurt. How about you?

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.380
It's everywhere. The whole 
neighborhood's gray.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:31.160
It makes me feel blue.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.160
Let's deploy the Urahara.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:33.990
Yeah.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.380
What should we do, Rito?

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:47.480
I can't believe the color is 
disappearing from Harajuku.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.090
<i>Rito-chan, Mari-chan! Down here!</i>

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.760
<i>Hey!</i>

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.760
What is that?

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.030
A cake.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.770
Aren't the colors a little too plain?

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.120
Did you invent some kind of weaponized cake?

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:07.360
Oh, that could be a good idea!

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:13.290
Hmm... How about a cake that's delicious, 
but explodes when you throw it?

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.640
Just so you know, I was joking.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.440
I was joking, too.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:21.210
If you're joking, at least 
make it sound like one!

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:22.990
Hey, Kotoko.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:26.190
It's that color because 
of the Scoopers, right?

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:30.510
Yeah. Looks like that bird thing got to it.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.980
I'm sorry, indeed.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:36.120
If only we'd been able 
to chase it away sooner...

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.470
I'm terribly sorry.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.330
It's not your fault.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:44.700
Don't worry about it.

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:46.230
I'm glad you weren't hurt.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:49.690
Okay... indeed.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:55.000
So? Kotoko, I thought 
you had something to do.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.180
Don't tell me you came to deliver that cake?

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:01.710
Well, I analyzed the cake,

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:05.420
and its composition is totally unchanged.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:08.920
It's delicious, too.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.630
Just like the recipe.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.740
Everyone loves these cute cakes,

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:17.440
but just changing the color makes it 
look like something else. Who knew?

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:18.580
Sorry, Kotoko.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:19.850
Could you cut to the chase?

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.270
Okay.

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:27.440
First, I think this cake 
had its color stolen.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.120
The Scoopers are after our culture, right?

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:36.280
I think these are collecting 
color rather than culture.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.470
So they're just taking colors and 
leaving the objects unscathed.

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.210
But this isn't our Harajuku.

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:50.780
It's awful, indeed.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:55.630
Kotoko, is there any way 
to get the colors back?

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:59.920
We haven't encountered these Scoopers 
before, so I don't have enough data.

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:05.190
It's impossible to restore something 
that's been physically destroyed.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:09.380
But these have had their color stolen 
using some kind of special power,

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:13.540
so it's possible the effects can 
be reversed if we beat them.

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:14.070
Got it.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:16.140
This'll be a good workout.

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:19.050
I'll help you, indeed!

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:19.740
What?!

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:20.630
Huh?

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:26.080
I love the colorful and 
sparkly Harajuku, indeed.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:29.500
What they're doing is terrible, indeed.

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:34.300
Misa-chan really loves Harajuku, huh?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.880
We understand how you feel, but...

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:41.000
Misa-sama, you don't have 
any combat abilities.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.120
You'll only get in their way.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:46.880
Misa-chan, thanks.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:51.940
But it'd be terrible if you got 
hurt, so wait someplace safe.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:54.650
We'll get Harajuku's color back.

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:57.360
Okay, indeed.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:02.260
Let's start by searching this area.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:03.320
Okay.

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:13.580
You had me sweating bullets earlier.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:17.460
But it's mine...

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:20.820
How could they...

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:28.860
do that to my sparklies?

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:44.530
Mari!

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:55.210
<b>Warning</b>

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:03.950
Mari-chan, are you okay?

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:04.620
Yeah.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.020
All right!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.500
The blade's more effective 
against the big ones.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:23.470
I think we can beat the little ones 
with Mari-chan's rapid-fire mode.

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:26.370
Yeah, but look.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:33.620
Was there a sale today?

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:35.130
I don't think so.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:37.250
Let's get out of here.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:38.520
Agreed.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:00.740
Mari, Kotoko, let's head into that alley.

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:11.120
They're stuck.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:13.290
Now's our chance!

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:31.140
We've beaten most of them by now, haven't we?

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:33.150
Yeah.

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:37.270
About 10% of them.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:39.960
What? That's all?

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.250
There's no end to them.

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.240
Huh?

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:43.830
My radar...

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:51.160
How cute!

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:54.720
It's hard to see them as cute right now.

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:56.140
Fly up.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:07.240
I'm glad they're flightless birds.

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:10.940
Looks like those penguins 
are trying to get us.

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.900
I agree.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:17.980
Maybe it's because our colorful Urahara 
version clothes stand out in Harajuku.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:21.530
They're trying to steal the color 
in our clothes and belongings?

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.000
Maybe.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.900
Then that solves our problem.

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:28.660
If we just keep walking, 
they'll follow us. Right?

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:29.740
I think so.

00:13:30.230 --> 00:13:32.700
In that case, there's 
something I want to try.

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:44.340
It's dangerous by the window.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.000
I'll be fine, indeed.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:47.940
You're not fine!

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:50.220
Need I remind you that you are human?

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.260
What's happening?

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:01.490
It's beautiful, indeed.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:25.330
Rito seems to be having fun.

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:27.660
And her plan is amazing.

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:32.240
Just like she planned, they're all gathering 
around the color in her drawings.

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:40.060
Birds incoming!

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:42.890
You won't get in Rito's way!

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:47.000
Way to go, Mari-chan!

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.650
Kotoko, are you ready?

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:49.570
Yeah, perfect.

00:14:55.670 --> 00:15:00.320
I had no idea the Amatsumara 
could be used that way.

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:06.380
Such creative people do unexpected things.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:10.010
They're so cute, indeed!

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:11.490
This is the last stroke.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:19.540
There.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.870
Kotoko, the rest is up to you.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:41.840
Okay!

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:43.690
Here I go.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:44.170
There.

00:15:57.610 --> 00:16:02.760
Kotoko, I think I'll avoid 
fighting with you from now on.

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:03.860
What?

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.440
Mari-chan, you're too nice.

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:07.200
I'd never fight with you.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:10.180
Just so you know, that was a joke.

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:12.400
I was joking too, of course.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:17.300
I told you, make it sound 
like a joke if you're joking!

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:17.880
<i>Sheesh!</i>

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:19.660
<i>Mari-chan, your face is red.</i>

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:21.070
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:24.480
Kotoko, the Scoopers are acting strange.

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:26.380
They're not turning into sweets.

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:28.120
You're right.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:30.680
Rito-chan, come back to us.

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:31.410
<i>Okay.</i>

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:22.610
I won't let them take our color.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:23.310
Yeah.

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:27.240
Rito-chan, that one's slow, 
but it seems powerful.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:28.270
Be careful!

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:29.410
Got it.

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:56.970
I'll handle the little ones.

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:02.760
<i>Mari-chan, shoot its belly with your cannon.</i>

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:03.700
Okay!

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:29.570
Looks like that one's the boss.

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:31.320
I guess it's my turn.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:51.320
I don't see any Scooper signals left in the city.

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:52.560
Really?

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:55.300
I'm not interested in visiting 
the Harajuku safari park again.

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:58.530
Don't worry. I don't joke.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:18:59.980
Yeah, right.

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:04.200
<i>I'm glad the color's back.</i>

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:28.020
Everything's sparkling again, indeed.

00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:30.770
Yeah! So is Sayumin's shop.

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:33.520
Welcome.

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:38.650
Thank you.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:42.490
Yes, the weather's great again today.

00:19:57.410 --> 00:19:59.340
Good idea, Rito.

00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:03.930
Now, if we ever feel depressed, 
we can just look at the sky.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:08.970
I thought a gray sky didn't 
really suit Harajuku.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:11.020
Hey!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.240
Rito-chan, Mari-chan!

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:18.480
Let's have lunch, indeed!

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:24.100
Here, Mari-chan.

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:25.410
Thanks.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:28.490
I guess the way a cake looks 
really does matter.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:31.180
There's such a thing as tasty colors.

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:33.520
And Harajuku-esque colors, indeed.

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:44.360
What a beautiful sky, indeed.

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:48.720
Then I'll give you some Misa-chan-esque 
colors as a present.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.460
A present?

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:53.180
Whisper, whisper.

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:57.160
Here.

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:04.430
How cute.

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:06.530
It's perfect for you, Misa-chan.

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:12.750
I've never felt so happy before, indeed.

00:21:14.010 --> 00:21:15.710
I'm glad you like it.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.110
It's so cute, indeed!

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:22.620
Huh?

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:25.430
These sparklies look familiar...

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.330
Yeah. I made it with those beads.

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:37.660
Amazing!

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:40.980
It's so cute when all the sparklies 
are put together, indeed!

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:45.630
You three really, really are amazing, indeed!

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:51.300
I love you, indeed!

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:27.250
I wanna eat one!

00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:29.040
Miss Misa, what's wrong?

00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:31.120
I want to eat the center of a donut.

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:33.020
I've never seen one before.

00:23:33.020 --> 00:23:34.640
I'm going to ask Rito to make one for me.

00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:37.360
I'm coming too, Rito-sama!
